      "text": "<|channel|>analysis<|message|>We need to write a simple website in HTML. When user clicks the button, it shows a random joke from a list of 4 jokes. So we need some HTML page with a button, maybe a div for the joke. Use JavaScript to handle the click, random selection. Need to choose jokes. Provide full HTML code. Possibly we can use vanilla JS. Provide style minimal. Provide explanation at top? The user said \"Write a simple website in HTML.\" So just code. Provide nice representation. Use <script> at bottom. Let's produce final answer.<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>Here’s a minimal, self‑contained HTML page that displays a random joke from a list of four jokes each time the button is pressed.  \nCopy the code into a file named `index.html` and open it in a browser.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Random Joke Generator</title>\n<style>\n  body {font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem;}\n  #joke {margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.2rem; color:#333;}\n  button {padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem; font-size: 1rem; cursor: pointer;}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>Need a Laugh?</h1>\n<button id=\"jokeBtn\">Tell me a joke!</button>\n<p id=\"joke\"></p>\n\n<script>\n  // Array of jokes\n  const jokes = [\n    \"Why don’t skeletons fight each other? They don’t have the guts.\",\n    \"Parallel lines have so much in common… it’s a shame they’ll never meet.\",\n    \"I told my wife she was drawing her eyebrows too high. She looked surprised.\",\n    \"What do you call a fake noodle? An impasta.\"\n  ];\n\n  // Grab DOM elements\n  const btn = document.getElementById('jokeBtn');\n  const jokeEl = document.getElementById('joke');\n\n  // Function to show a random joke\n  function showRandomJoke() {\n    const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);\n    jokeEl.textContent = jokes[randomIndex];\n  }\n\n  // Attach event listener\n  btn.addEventListener('click', showRandomJoke);\n</script>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. The page contains a button (`#jokeBtn`) and a paragraph (`#joke`) where the joke will appear.  \n2. A JavaScript array (`jokes`) holds the four jokes.  \n3. When the button is clicked, the `showRandomJoke` function picks a random index, picks the corresponding joke, and updates the paragraph’s text.  \n\nFeel free to add more jokes or tweak the styling to suit your taste!",
